[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says *one issue, one fix queued*. Its own table says otherwise. The
reports were merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and
every subject in #4471 is some way of saying "wrong date". That is the symptom, not the cause.
#4471 holds two problems. Each now has its own ticket:

1. [`parser`: the shared parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/BorislavStefanov31/support-kb-4471/issues/1)
2. [`hint`: the booking-v3 form hints `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants](https://github.com/BorislavStefanov31/support-kb-4471/issues/2)

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued fix for the month-first parser closes only the first ticket. The hint keeps sending
flipped dates after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Read the table by row: **`parser`** is ticket 1 and **`hint`** is ticket 2. The table marks
`hint` *no ticket of its own*; it has one now.

## The two problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first. A date like 7/4 is read as 4 July, so bookings, invites and reminders land on a day with
day and month swapped. Only dates with both parts at 12 or below can flip, which is why some
months look fine. Reports come from every tenant and every channel.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** Tenants on booking-v3
who write the day first get bookings through that form typed month first, as the hint asks, and
read the tenant's way. The symptom is the same swap, so subject lines cannot tell it apart; only
form bookings at booking-v3 tenants have it. Fixing the parser does not fix the hint. Intake tags
were guessed from the reporter's browser and disagree with the cause in both directions, as the
*tagged as* column shows; do not triage on them.

The note under the table counts the reports the desk read as a one-day move. They stay in
`parser`, where they were filed. If they keep coming after the parser fix, they are worth a look
of their own.

## For the desk

- Triage date reports on tenant and booking path, not subject. `causes.ts` already knows how.
- Decision 0001 merged these two into one ticket. It needs a new decision record to replace it.

